## Data Flow Descriptions

### 1. Application Startup
```
User Opens Browser
    → Next.js App Loads (Static Export from Firebase Hosting)
    → Middleware Runs (Security Headers, Auth Check)
    → AuthProvider Initializes (Supabase Client)
    → TanStack Query Client Created
    → Dashboard Page Renders (Server Component)
```

### 2. User Authentication (Login)
```
User Submits Login Form
    → POST /api/auth/login (Next.js API Route)
    → Prisma: Find User by Email (PostgreSQL)
    → bcrypt: Compare Password Hash
    → Create HMAC-Signed Session Cookie (alex_local_session)
    → Return User Data + Set Cookie
    → AuthProvider Refreshes (Supabase Auth State)
    → Redirect to /dashboard
```

### 3. Authenticated API Request (Firebase Callable Function)
```
Frontend Component Calls Function (e.g., aiFunctions.sendMessage)
    → Firebase Functions SDK Sends HTTPS Callable Request
    → Firebase Verifies Auth Token (request.auth.uid)
    → Function Executes (e.g., ai.ts:sendMessage)
    → Function Accesses Firestore (db.collection)
    → Function Calls AI Provider (OpenAI/NVIDIA/etc.)
    → Function Writes Response to Firestore
    → Function Returns Result to Frontend
    → TanStack Query Updates Cache
    → Component Re-renders with Data
```

### 4. Document Upload & Processing
```
User Uploads File (document-upload.tsx)
    → POST /api/documents (API Route) OR documentFunctions.createDocument (Callable)
    → Get Signed Upload URL from Firebase Storage
    → Upload File Directly to Storage (Client → Storage)
    → Confirm Upload (documentFunctions.confirmUpload)
    → Storage Trigger (onDocumentUpload) Creates Processing Job
    → Processing Pipeline (DocumentProcessingJob):
        → Extract Text (pdf-parse, mammoth, Tesseract OCR)
        → Chunk Text (chunker.ts)
        → Generate Embeddings (OpenAI text-embedding-3-small)
        → Store Chunks + Embeddings in Firestore (documentChunks)
        → Update Document Status to READY
```

### 5. RAG Query (AI Chat with Documents)
```
User Sends Message (rag-chat.tsx)
    → POST /api/rag/query (API Route) OR ragFunctions.ragQuery (Callable)
    → Get User's AI Credentials (Decrypt API Key)
    → Generate Query Embedding (OpenAI)
    → Semantic Search in Firestore (documentChunks with embeddings)
    → Build Context from Top-K Chunks
    → Add Memories, Academic Context, Conversation History
    → Call AI Provider (NVIDIA/OpenAI/Gemini/Anthropic)
    → Stream/Return Answer with Citations
    → Save Conversation + Messages to Firestore/PostgreSQL
    → Return Response to Frontend
```

### 6. AI Credentials Management
```
User Adds AI API Key (ai-settings/page.tsx)
    → POST /api/ai/credentials (API Route)
    → Encrypt API Key (AES-256-GCM with ENCRYPTION_KEY)
    → Hash Key (SHA-256 for Deduplication)
    → Store in PostgreSQL (AICredential) + Firestore (aiCredentials)
    → Set as Default if Requested
```

### 7. Attendance Marking (Lecturer)
```
Lecturer Opens Attendance Page
    → GET /api/attendance/sessions (API Route)
    → Lecturer Creates Session (attendanceFunctions.createSession)
    → Validates Lecturer Assignment (lecturerAssignments)
    → Creates Session + Pre-fills ABSENT Records for All Enrolled Students
    → Lecturer Marks Attendance (attendanceFunctions.markAttendance)
    → Batch Update Attendance Records
    → Scheduled Function Checks Daily for Low Attendance (<35%)
```

### 8. Error Handling & Logging
```
Function Errors
    → Caught in Try/Catch
    → HttpsError Thrown (Standard Codes: unauthenticated, permission-denied, not-found, failed-precondition)
    → Frontend Catches Error (TanStack Query onError)
    → Toast Notification Shown (use-toast hook)
    → Console Error Logged (Structured Logging in Functions)
    → Optional: Sentry Integration (SENTRY_DSN)
```

### 9. Deployment Flow
```
Push to Main Branch
    → GitHub Actions Triggered
    → Install Dependencies (pnpm)
    → Lint (ESLint)
    → Typecheck (TypeScript)
    → Test (Jest)
    → Build (Next.js Static Export + Functions TSC)
    → Deploy Preview Channel (Firebase Hosting)
    → Manual Approval for Production
    → Deploy to Production (Firebase Hosting + Functions)
    → Secrets Injected from Secret Manager
```